---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information"
  description="Our position on selling and sharing personal information, and how to exercise your privacy rights."
>
  <h2>1. Our position</h2>
  <p>
    We do <strong>not</strong> sell personal information. We also do not share personal information for cross-context
    behavioural advertising. We do not use advertising cookies or third-party advertising trackers.
  </p>
  <p>
    The information you submit through the quote form is sent to the reseller you selected so they can respond to
    your request. That delivery is a service you requested, not a sale or advertising share.
  </p>

  <h2>2. California privacy rights</h2>
  <p>If you are a California resident, you may have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Know</strong> what categories of personal information we collect, use, and disclose.</li>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> the specific pieces of personal information we hold about you.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete</strong> personal information we collected from you, subject to legal exceptions.</li>
    <li><strong>Correct</strong> inaccurate personal information.</li>
    <li><strong>Opt out</strong> of the sale or sharing of personal information. We do not sell or share it.</li>
    <li><strong>Limit</strong> the use of sensitive personal information. We do not collect sensitive personal information for inferring characteristics.</li>
    <li><strong>Non-discrimination</strong> for exercising your privacy rights.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Categories of information</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Category</th>
        <th>Examples</th>
        <th>Disclosed to</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Identifiers</td>
        <td>Name, email address</td>
        <td>Selected reseller; service providers</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Commercial information</td>
        <td>Products and configuration you request</td>
        <td>Selected reseller; service providers</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Internet or network activity</td>
        <td>User agent, IP-derived country, hashed IP for rate limiting</td>
        <td>Service providers</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Communications</td>
        <td>Subject and message you submit</td>
        <td>Selected reseller; service providers</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>We do not sell these categories, and we do not share them for cross-context behavioural advertising.</p>

  <h2>4. How to submit a request</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:contact@davisweatherstation.com">contact@davisweatherstation.com</a> with the subject
    “Privacy Request” and describe what you want to access, correct, or delete. You may also use the{' '}
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Verification</h2>
  <p>
    We may ask for information needed to verify your identity and the request, such as confirming control of the
    email address used for the submission. We will use verification information only for that purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Authorized agents</h2>
  <p>
    You may use an authorized agent to submit a request. We may require written permission and may still contact you
    directly to confirm the request, as permitted by law.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Response timing</h2>
  <p>
    We aim to respond within 45 days of a verifiable request. If we need more time, we will tell you why and extend
    the period as permitted by law.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Other regions</h2>
  <p>
    Visitors in the EU, UK, and other regions may have similar rights under their local laws. See our{' '}
    <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:contact@davisweatherstation.com">contact@davisweatherstation.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
